  <iati-identifier>GB-GOV-1-300596-101</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="GB-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK - Foreign, Commonwealth Development Office (FCDO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Preparation for Strengthening Governance for Transformational Change in Water Security</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project preparation phase will develop a strong evidence-based multi-year strategy which supports strengthening governance and increasing investment in sustainable water use in land-based value chains to increase resilience and environmental benefits for people,&#xa0;nature, and climate. The project preparatory phase provides the opportunity to outline a coordinated approach for strategic alignment, integration, and connectivity of the three existing workstreams, and to ensure that through collaboration these workstreams are strengthened, scaled-up, and implemented in a coordinated manner. The main outcome of this period is the design of a multi-year work program which includes the Water Tracker, Resilient Water Accelerator, and Fair Water Footprint workstreams, and addresses the vision and objectives of the larger SGWC program. Over the course of the project preparatory period, partners from the three initiatives will work together to further define our strategic alignment, including in the following areas:

The most useful governance and project finance structures required to ensure strong and cost-effective delivery of the overall programme goal and the three areas of work.
Methods to maximize stakeholder and geographical alignment where appropriate and relevant for greatest impact.
How to embed monitoring, evaluation and learning both within and across the three programs, and within FCDO learning structures and processes, to effectively create a programme &#x2018;learning cycle&#x2019;.
How partnership across the consortia can support detecting, avoiding, and reducing potential risk factors across the programmatic areas.

This project preparatory phase will also include implementation of initiative specific activities under workstream, where those activities contribute to building the evidence base of the initiative individually, while also exploring further opportunities for alignment between the Water Tracker, RWA, and FWF.</narrative>
  </description>
